\[n\sigma=\frac{1}{R}\times\frac{dE/dx_{measured}}{dE/dx_{theory}}, \tag{3.2}\]

where \(dE/dx\) is the specific ionization energy loss per unit path length and \(R\) is the \(dE/dx\) resolution. The black line corresponds to Bichsel function for kaons. The basic cuts for kaons selection using TPC are listed in the table 3.2.

