-wider centrality bins like for example \(0-80\%\). There is another approach, known as event by event resolution correction, for event plane resolution correction for wide centrality bin [10]. In this method resolution correction for wide centrality bin has been done by dividing the term \(\cos(2(\phi-\Psi))\) by the event plane resolution (R) for the corresponding centrality for each event.

\[\langle v_{2}\rangle=\langle\frac{v_{2}^{obs}}{R}\rangle. \tag{3.17}\]

These two method do not give same \(\langle v_{2}\rangle\) because

\[\frac{\langle v_{2}^{obs}\rangle}{\langle R\rangle}\neq\langle\frac{v_{2}^{ obs}}{R}\rangle. \tag{3.18}\]

