#### Uncertainty from residual background

The shape of residual background after mixed event subtraction varies with \(p_{T}\). This is because of contamination in kaon selection using the dE/dx information. Using only dE/dx information one can identify kaon with high purity up-to momentum 0.6 GeV/\(c\). So with increase in \(p_{T}\), the contamination in kaon sample from pion and proton increases. To estimate the effect different methods has been used for raw \(\phi\) yield extraction.

